    "answer": "Done — the task succeeded on the first attempt.\n\n**What ran:** a single JavaScript run using `noe:http`'s `serve` and `fetch` on `127.0.0.1` with port 0 (OS-assigned), so it bound temporary port **37069**.\n\n- The handler read the POSTed JSON `{value: 21}` and returned `Response.json({value: 42})` (doubling the input).\n- The client POSTed `{value:21}` as JSON, consumed the full response body via `await response.text()`, then parsed it.\n- Verified `status === 200` and `value === 42` (both checks passed; a mismatch would have thrown).\n- The listener was released in a `finally` block, so it closes even on failure; `server.close()` ran after the response was fully consumed, outside the handler.\n- Only the loopback URL `server.url` was contacted — no other network destinations.\n\n**report.json** (written to the working directory, numeric fields):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": 200,\n  \"value\": 42,\n  \"port\": 37069\n}\n```\n\n`port` is the actual listening port reported by the server handle after binding.",
    "binary_sha256": "488a6f47bfac7967c80e18582534527a38940c24906c194a6a5c80743b24894f",
    "artifacts": "/tmp/noe-stdlib-step3-20261019-84fpyjw_/live-smoke",
    "tools": [
